It says two hours and six minutes

00:52:01.490 --> 00:52:03.203
would get us in at 3:19.

00:52:05.130 --> 00:52:07.970
- I've got 86 miles on my bike.

00:52:07.970 --> 00:52:09.093
- I've got 83.

00:52:10.293 --> 00:52:12.010
- Okay, so we'll
definitely have to plug in.

00:52:12.010 --> 00:52:12.903
- Yeah.
- Nice.

00:52:15.210 --> 00:52:17.620
But at least we won't have
to do it for very long,

00:52:17.620 --> 00:52:20.670
you know, half an hour, 40
minutes will be enough I reckon.

00:52:20.670 --> 00:52:22.193
- Yeah.

00:52:22.193 --> 00:52:24.860
(wind rustling)

00:53:01.140 --> 00:53:02.120
- Wow, we're above the clouds.

00:53:02.120 --> 00:53:04.654
Oh my gosh, look at this.

00:53:04.654 --> 00:53:06.760
The change in scenery, it's just...

00:53:08.465 --> 00:53:10.465
It's just extraordinary.

00:53:11.740 --> 00:53:13.740
It's become quite arid now, you know,

00:53:13.740 --> 00:53:16.780
sort of that bit in between
desert and jungle where,

00:53:16.780 --> 00:53:21.183
you know, all the trees here
are much lower and shorter

00:53:21.183 --> 00:53:23.833
and you know, 'cause everything
takes longer to grow.

00:53:25.810 --> 00:53:30.810
And it's really quite pretty.

00:53:31.070 --> 00:53:34.440
And the rolling hills, it's very,

00:53:34.440 --> 00:53:36.190
I think it's very different to what

00:53:37.382 --> 00:53:39.883
it was not that long ago, you know?

00:53:41.690 --> 00:53:45.500
We were just in lush
vegetation, very humid.

00:53:45.500 --> 00:53:49.020
This has become quite arid and dry and...

00:53:49.880 --> 00:53:52.333
But it still has this real
beauty and totally different,

00:53:52.333 --> 00:53:56.133
too, to what we've been used to so far.

00:53:57.110 --> 00:54:01.153
So, it's really really pretty cool.

00:54:02.600 --> 00:54:04.203
What a beautiful country,
lovely people as well.

00:54:04.203 --> 00:54:06.870
I mean, we just had the
most amazing experience

00:54:06.870 --> 00:54:11.230
in the very first solar
farm here in Honduras

00:54:14.170 --> 00:54:16.860
and they're doing some
20 watts right beside

00:54:16.860 --> 00:54:21.860
a big power station that
burns heavy oil, or that,

00:54:22.317 --> 00:54:25.713
you know, the slop after
that processing oil.

00:54:26.550 --> 00:54:27.703
And they do 240.

00:54:30.760 --> 00:54:32.470
But, you know, it was
just done and they said

00:54:32.470 --> 00:54:35.660
that what they're trying to
do here in the next two years

00:54:35.660 --> 00:54:40.660
is to try and become at least 50% reliant

00:54:41.418 --> 00:54:45.160
on renewable resources and
they've got lots and lots

00:54:45.160 --> 00:54:48.680
of different solar panel
farms and wind farms

00:54:48.680 --> 00:54:51.650
and hydroelectric.

00:54:51.650 --> 00:54:53.840
So they're really doing their bid.

00:54:53.840 --> 00:54:55.278
And this country this small,

00:54:55.278 --> 00:54:57.900
they need to look after themselves.

00:54:57.900 --> 00:55:02.090
And the guy was super
keen to show us all about

00:55:03.110 --> 00:55:08.110
what his little baby is doing
and what they're producing.

00:55:08.570 --> 00:55:10.883
So, it's really lucky and lovely to see

00:55:10.883 --> 00:55:13.100
and the really nice thing
about the whole thing

00:55:13.100 --> 00:55:15.860
was that we were managed
to park up and we managed

00:55:15.860 --> 00:55:19.223
to get, you know, half
an hour's charge up.

00:55:19.223 --> 00:55:21.855
You know, we got four of 5% I think.

00:55:21.855 --> 00:55:23.520
It's a little tough turn coming up-

00:55:23.520 --> 00:55:24.700
- Yeah.

00:55:24.700 --> 00:55:27.743
